# Cite-ready software citation for Vermithor / VU-Bench.
# GitHub "Cite this repository" reads this file. No DOI is registered yet.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use Vermithor or VU-Bench, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
title: Vermithor (VU-Bench)
abstract: >-
  Vermithor Understanding Bench (VU-Bench) is a small understanding harness
  for PDE surrogates. Four exams (Predict, Conserve, Counterfactual, Explain)
  score whether a model has grasped the dynamics of viscous Burgers (1D) and
  heat (2D), not just interpolated training trajectories. v0.1.0 packages the
  Week 1–4 scaffold: classical finite-difference labels, laptop-scale FNO and
  PINO-style baselines, OOD probes, fail-closed trust flags, a pinned Exam 4
  item set, and SHA dataset pins. Reports contain only measured numbers;
  missing checkpoints stay not_trained.
authors:
  - family-names: Pathan
    given-names: Shehbaz
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-12"
url: "https://github.com/shehbaz0101/vermithor"
repository-code: "https://github.com/shehbaz0101/vermithor"
keywords:
  - Vermithor
  - VU-Bench
  - PDE
  - surrogate
  - Fourier neural operator
  - PINO
  - understanding harness
